From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jaime Dias <jaimejosediasnt@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 30 Aug 2026 00:00:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] amigavideo: wait for the frame on the beam, not only on the
 interrupt

waitvblank() spun on csd->framecounter, which is moved by exactly one
thing: gfx_vblank, the server this driver installs with
AddIntServer(INTB_VERTB) in initcustom(). Nothing else can end the loop.

resetmode() is its only caller, and both of resetmode's callers mean
"there is nothing visible, blank the display" -- which is true before the
driver has finished starting up, and therefore before that server
exists. The loop then spins on a counter nothing can move,
initialisation never returns, and OpenLibrary("amigavideo.hidd") hands
the AmigaVideo task a NULL. On Bellatrix that is a machine frozen at one
address for the rest of the boot, with the display already handed over
so nothing is visible either.

The beam is the other witness and the better one: a register read, so it
needs no interrupt, no server and no enabled interrupt level, and it is
what the hardware offers for exactly this. Both are kept -- where the
interrupt works it still ends the wait first -- and a counter guards the
case where neither moves, so an unprogrammed chipset costs a wrong frame
instead of the machine.
---
 .../hidd/amigavideo/amigavideo_chipset.c      | 45 ++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 42 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/m68k-amiga/hidd/amigavideo/amigavideo_chipset.c b/arch/m68k-amiga/hidd/amigavideo/amigavideo_chipset.c
--- a/arch/m68k-amiga/hidd/amigavideo/amigavideo_chipset.c
+++ b/arch/m68k-amiga/hidd/amigavideo/amigavideo_chipset.c
@@ -69,13 +69,54 @@
     custom->vposw = 0x8000;
     custom->color[0] = DEFAULT_BORDER_GRAY;
 }
 
+/*
+ * Wait one frame -- on the beam as well as on the interrupt.
+ *
+ * This was "// ugly busy loop for now.." spinning on csd->framecounter alone,
+ * and the counter is moved by exactly one thing: gfx_vblank, the server this
+ * driver installs with AddIntServer(INTB_VERTB) in initcustom(). Nothing else
+ * can end the loop.
+ *
+ * That is a dependency the loop cannot check and must not have. resetmode()
+ * is its only caller and both of its callers mean "there is nothing visible,
+ * blank the display" -- which is true before the driver has finished starting
+ * up, and therefore before that server exists. The loop then spins on a
+ * counter nothing can move, initialisation never returns, and
+ * OpenLibrary("amigavideo.hidd") hands the AmigaVideo task a NULL. On
+ * Bellatrix that was a machine frozen at one address for the rest of the
+ * boot.
+ *
+ * The beam is the other witness, and the better one: it is a register read,
+ * so it needs no interrupt, no server, and no enabled interrupt level, and it
+ * is what the hardware itself offers for exactly this. VPOSR bit 0 and the
+ * top byte of VHPOSR are the line counter; it only ever decreases when a new
+ * frame starts, so one decrease is one frame.
+ *
+ * Both witnesses are kept. Where the interrupt works it still ends the wait
+ * first, so nothing that relied on it changes; where it cannot, the beam
+ * does. The counter guards the case where neither moves -- an unprogrammed or
+ * stopped chipset -- so the worst outcome is a wrong frame instead of a dead
+ * machine.
+ */
 static VOID waitvblank(struct amigavideo_staticdata *csd)
 {
-    // ugly busy loop for now..
+    volatile struct Custom *custom = (struct Custom*)0xdff000;
     UWORD fc = csd->framecounter;
-    while (fc == csd->framecounter);
+    UWORD line = (UWORD)(((custom->vposr & 1) << 8) | (custom->vhposr >> 8));
+    ULONG guard = 0;
+
+    while (fc == csd->framecounter) {
+        UWORD now = (UWORD)(((custom->vposr & 1) << 8) | (custom->vhposr >> 8));
+
+        if (now < line)
+            break;              /* the beam wrapped: a frame has passed */
+        line = now;
+
+        if (++guard > 4000000)
+            break;              /* neither witness moves; do not hang here */
+    }
 }
  
 static VOID setnullsprite(struct amigavideo_staticdata *csd)
 {
